            "summary": "This document describes a case involving a 45-year-old man who recently began treatment with Glucoreg for his type 2 diabetes. After taking the medication in the morning, he experienced mild nausea and vomiting about one hour post-dose, which occurred on multiple days. Although the symptoms were bothersome, they did not necessitate medical intervention. \n\nTo address the side effects, the timing of the medication was modified so he took it with food. Following this adjustment, the patient's symptoms improved significantly. \n\nThe document is relevant to a patient safety review as it reports an adverse reaction to Glucoreg, specifically gastrointestinal symptoms. Additionally, it provides insights into how adjusting the timing of medication intake can mitigate side effects, highlighting the importance of patient education and management in pharmacotherapy. Overall, this case emphasizes the importance of monitoring patient responses to medications and making necessary adjustments to enhance safety and treatment outcomes.",
